  data: {
    LLM: "Count your winners (Aces/Kings). Count your trumps. If you have 5 trumps, you can usually win 3-4 tricks. Don't overbid on Queens unless you hold the King/Ace.\n\nCovering a Nil: If your partner bids Nil, your job is to take every trick they might accidentally win. Lead low to them so they can duck. Trump if necessary to save them.\n\nBag Management: If you are way ahead, take bags to force opponents to react. If you are close to 10 bags (-100), try to duck tricks or let opponents win cheap ones.",
